# Swarm operational logs / status snapshots — diagnostics only, ~89 MB of
# append-only churn. The app reads these off the local /mnt/main disk, never
# from GitHub, and no download needs them. The swarm now snapshots them to
# the `telemetry` branch (hourly, off-box backup) instead of main. See
# github_push_truth_log() / _maybe_push_telemetry_branch() in swarm/swarm_v4_1.py.
master_truth_log.jsonl
wonder_log.jsonl
truth_lattice_log.jsonl
cost_log.jsonl
memory_palace.jsonl
swarm_status.json
master_status.json
context_cache.json
# tier2_digest.txt was rewritten every ~90s right before each push, making it
# the last file that forced a "🦅 v4.1 auto-push" commit to main almost every
# cycle. Every consumer reads it off local disk, never GitHub. truth_debt_
# ledger.jsonl is an append-only log. Both now go to the telemetry branch;
# the rendered insights/truth_debt_report.md stays on main. (2026-09-04)
tier2_digest.txt
truth_debt_ledger.jsonl
# Gzipped older log lines trimmed off the above by the swarm's daily
# maybe_trigger_log_rotation() - local-only, never pushed anywhere.
log_archive/

# Personal/sensitive local data - this repo is PUBLIC, never commit these.
# Reviewed and deliberately excluded 2026-08-24; locked here so a future
# `git add -A` can't sweep them in by accident.
institute_memory/EIN_confirmation.pdf
institute_memory/org_facts.txt
USER_CONTEXT.md
memory/
conversations/
agent_runs/
